<MultiLineNote>
If you use the `and` operator, only one media type for a media query can be included.
</MultiLineNote>

#### 2.1.1 Not

The `not` operator is a Media Query Modifier. It negates the entire Media Query result.

<MultiLineNote>
If you use the `not` operator, you must also specify a media type.
</MultiLineNote>

#### Wrong Syntax

```css|UGLY
@media not (min-width: 600px) and (max-width: 800px) {
       /* CSS rules go here */
}
```

#### Correct Syntax

```css|CLEAN
@media not screen and (min-width: 600px) {
     /* CSS rules go here */
}
```

